{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>You shall not sow your vineyard with diverse seeds.</b> Our Rabbis, of blessed memory, received that one is not liable until he sows wheat and barley and grape-seed in a single hand-throw, and this is the force of 'לא תזרע כרמך כלאים' — 'your vineyard' is the grape-seed; 'diverse seeds' are wheat and barley. Our Rabbis, of blessed memory, deduced this from the fact that it is written 'כרמך כלאים' and it did not say 'כרמך לא תזרע כלאים' as it said (Leviticus 19:19) 'שדך לא תזרע כלאים'; for had it said so, I would understand 'your vineyard' — that is, sown with grape-seed — 'you shall not sow it with diverse seeds,' which are wheat and barley. But now that it says 'כרמך כלאים,' one must understand that he sows the sowing of the grape-seed and the diverse seeds together; if so, he is not liable until he sows wheat and barley and grape-seed in a single hand-throw, according to what our Rabbis, of blessed memory, received. And one who sows wheat and barley and grape-seed in the Land receives two lashes, one for diverse seeds and one for the diverse vineyard; for diverse seeds one is liable only in the Land, but for the diverse vineyard, even outside the Land in this era one is liable by Rabbinic decree, since the Torah was strict with them regarding the prohibition of benefit in the Land, as it says 'פן תקדש,' and our Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded 'פן תוקד אש.' And the reason for the prohibition of diverse kinds — its secret is the mingling of the supernal forces on high, and I have already elaborated on the verse 'את חקותי תשמרו' (Leviticus 19:19) in the section 'קדושים תהיו.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:50:12.364197060Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}